# Test: daemon start refuses control-plane-protection (copp) under firewall backend vpp before any plugin starts.
# Question: does `ze start` refuse a `control-plane-protection` block under
#           `interface backend vpp` and `firewall backend vpp` via the
#           `firewall-producer-tables` original-tree validator in `LoadConfig`,
#           exiting 1 before any plugin starts?
#           A unit test invokes `ValidateCustomSections` in isolation; only a
#           real daemon start proves the refusal occurs ahead of plugin start.
# VALIDATES: spec-dataplane-compatibility-guard AC-8 (copp at start) --
#            `firewall-producer-tables` translates `ze_copp` and rejects its
#            VPP-unsupported primitives in `LoadConfig` before startup begins.
# PREVENTS: CoPP under VPP passing boot load and failing only later inside
#           startup tier apply.

option=needs-build-tag:value=ze_vpp:state=present

stdin=ze-bgp:refused=config-validator-unavailable:terminator=EOF_CONF
interface {
	backend vpp;
}
firewall {
	backend vpp;
}
control-plane-protection {
	bgp {
		rate 100/second;
	}
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze -:stdin=ze-bgp:timeout=30s
expect=exit:code=1
expect=stderr:contains=error: load config:
expect=stderr:contains=ze_copp
expect=stderr:contains=not supported by backend vpp
reject=stderr:contains=interface backend loaded
reject=stderr:pattern=panic
